Build a mobile app: # BUILD A COMPLETE FULL-STACK APPLICATION: HRCONNECT

India-First HR Professional Consultation & Income Marketplace
You are acting as a senior product architect, UI/UX designer, full-stack engineer, database architect, security engineer and QA engineer.

Your task is to design and build a complete, functional, responsive, production-oriented MVP of HRConnect.

This is not a simple landing page, UI prototype, static website or generic HR software.

Build the actual application with a working frontend, backend, database, authentication, role-based permissions, expert marketplace, booking engine, payments, dashboards, notifications and admin management.

The application must be designed around one central business objective:

**Help HR professionals earn additional income by monetising their HR knowledge, skills and professional experience through paid consultations.**
Customers should be able to discover qualified HR professionals, understand their expertise, select consultation services, book appointments and pay online.

HR professionals should be able to create professional profiles, publish consultation services, manage their availability, receive bookings, consult customers and track their earnings.

HRConnect earns revenue by charging a commission on successful consultations.

# 1. PRODUCT VISION AND BUSINESS MODEL
What HRConnect actually does
HRConnect is an exclusive professional marketplace for HR expertise.

It connects two groups:

Supply side: HR professionals
Working HR professionals, independent HR consultants, HR leaders, recruiters and experienced people-management specialists can:

Register as HR experts.
Apply to become verified professionals.
Create detailed professional profiles.
Showcase their experience and expertise.
Publish paid consultation services.
Set their own consultation prices.
Define their weekly availability.
Accept paid consultation bookings.
Conduct consultations online.
Track completed consultations.
View earnings and platform commissions.
Request payouts.
Build a reputation through customer reviews.
The primary value proposition is that HR professionals can earn additional income from their existing knowledge without having to build an independent audience, become influencers or personally manage an entire customer acquisition system.

Demand side: Customers
Customers can include individuals, job seekers, employees, founders, startups and businesses.

They should be able to:

Browse HR professionals without registering.
Search for relevant expertise.
Filter professionals by category, price, experience and rating.
View detailed profiles.
Compare consultation services.
Select a consultation.
Choose an available date and time.
Register or sign in.
Complete payment.
Manage upcoming consultations.
Communicate necessary consultation details.
Submit reviews after completed sessions.
Platform revenue
HRConnect earns a percentage of successful consultation transactions.

Initial commission structure:

Platform-generated customer booking: 15% platform commission.
Expert-referred customer booking: 10% platform commission.
These percentages must be configurable by administrators.

The commission applicable to a booking must be snapshotted at the time of the transaction. Historical bookings must not change when future commission settings are updated.

All financial calculations must happen on the server.

